{
  "title": "React 21: GraphQL Clients",
  "subtitle": "React Explained",
  "audio": null,
  "beats": [
    {
      "id": "what",
      "min": 9,
      "duration": 15.0,
      "text": "REST vs GraphQL.",
      "visual": "compare",
      "left": {
        "title": "REST",
        "color": "blue",
        "items": [
          "Many endpoints",
          "Over- and under-fetching"
        ]
      },
      "right": {
        "title": "GraphQL",
        "color": "green",
        "items": [
          "One endpoint",
          "Ask for the exact fields"
        ]
      },
      "say": "With REST, each resource has its own endpoint, and you often get more or less data than a screen needs. With GraphQL there is one endpoint, and the client asks for exactly the fields it wants, across related data, in one request.",
      "voice": "/audio/react-21-graphql/what.wav"
    },
    {
      "id": "query",
      "min": 8,
      "duration": 11.0,
      "text": "A query.",
      "visual": "code",
      "items": [
        [
          "query {",
          "yellow"
        ],
        [
          "  user(id: 42) {",
          "blue"
        ],
        [
          "    name",
          "green"
        ],
        [
          "    posts { title }",
          "green"
        ],
        [
          "  }",
          "blue"
        ],
        [
          "}",
          "yellow"
        ]
      ],
      "say": "A query describes the shape of the data you want. The response mirrors it exactly: the user's name, and the titles of their posts, nothing more, in a single round trip.",
      "voice": "/audio/react-21-graphql/query.wav"
    },
    {
      "id": "hook",
      "min": 9,
      "duration": 12.0,
      "text": "Using it in a component.",
      "visual": "code",
      "items": [
        [
          "const { data, loading, error } =",
          "yellow"
        ],
        [
          "  useQuery(GET_USER, {",
          "blue"
        ],
        [
          "    variables: { id },",
          "green"
        ],
        [
          "  });",
          "blue"
        ],
        [
          "",
          "text"
        ],
        [
          "if (loading) return <Spinner />;",
          "pink"
        ]
      ],
      "say": "In React, a client library like Apollo gives you a use Query hook. You pass the query and its variables, and get back data, loading, and error, much like with TanStack Query.",
      "voice": "/audio/react-21-graphql/hook.wav"
    },
    {
      "id": "clients",
      "min": 9,
      "duration": 14.0,
      "text": "Choosing a client.",
      "visual": "chips",
      "items": [
        [
          "Apollo Client: full-featured",
          "blue"
        ],
        [
          "urql: lightweight, extensible",
          "green"
        ],
        [
          "Relay: fragments, scale",
          "yellow"
        ],
        [
          "TanStack Query + graphql-request",
          "pink"
        ]
      ],
      "say": "Apollo Client is the most feature-rich. urql is lighter and extensible. Relay is built for very large apps with fragments and strict conventions. And you can also use TanStack Query with a plain GraphQL request library.",
      "voice": "/audio/react-21-graphql/clients.wav"
    },
    {
      "id": "cache",
      "min": 10,
      "duration": 14.0,
      "text": "The normalized cache.",
      "visual": "flow",
      "badge": "UPDATE ONCE, EVERYWHERE",
      "items": [
        [
          "Response arrives",
          "yellow",
          "User 42, Post 7, Post 9"
        ],
        [
          "Normalize",
          "blue",
          "store by type and id"
        ],
        [
          "Cache entry User:42",
          "green",
          "shared by every query"
        ]
      ],
      "say": "GraphQL clients usually keep a normalized cache. Every object is stored once, by its type and I D. So when one query or mutation updates user forty-two, every screen showing that user updates automatically.",
      "voice": "/audio/react-21-graphql/cache.wav"
    },
    {
      "id": "tips",
      "min": 9,
      "duration": 13.5,
      "text": "Good habits.",
      "visual": "chips",
      "items": [
        [
          "Colocate queries with components",
          "green"
        ],
        [
          "Use fragments per component",
          "blue"
        ],
        [
          "Generate types from the schema",
          "yellow"
        ],
        [
          "Watch for N+1 on the server",
          "red"
        ]
      ],
      "say": "Keep each component's data needs next to it, with fragments. Generate TypeScript types from the schema so queries are checked, and remember the server side: naive resolvers can cause N plus one database queries.",
      "voice": "/audio/react-21-graphql/tips.wav"
    },
    {
      "id": "close",
      "min": 4,
      "duration": 4.5,
      "text": "Next: forms at scale.",
      "say": "Next up, forms at scale. Follow for more React.",
      "voice": "/audio/react-21-graphql/close.wav"
    }
  ]
}
